  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-51885",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The recursive formula is\n\n$$\nf(n+1)=3f(n),\n$$\n\nwhere $f(1)=-2.$\n\nWe use this formula to compute the terms $f(2),f(3),$ and $f(4)$ as follows:\n\n- To compute $f(2),$ we substitute $n=1$ into the recursive formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n+1) & =3f(n) \\\\ f(1+1) & =3f(1) \\\\ f(2) & =3f(1) \\\\ f(2) & =3(-2) \\\\ f(2) & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To compute $f(3),$ we substitute $n=2$ into the recursive formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n+1) & =3f(n) \\\\ f(2+1) & =3f(2) \\\\ f(3) & =3f(2) \\\\ f(3) & =3(-6) \\\\ f(3) & =-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- To compute $f(4),$ we substitute $n=3$ into the recursive formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(n+1) & =3f(n) \\\\ f(3+1) & =3f(3) \\\\ f(4) & =3f(3) \\\\ f(4) & =3(-18) \\\\ f(4) & =-54\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fourth term of the sequence is $f(4)=-54.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
